# Design tokens & accessibility

**Primary source:** Material 3 (`MaterialTheme`, `ColorScheme`,
`Typography`) for design tokens, plus Compose's semantics APIs
(`contentDescription`, `Modifier.semantics`, scalable `sp` text units)
and TalkBack — all Google-native.

**Community layer:** semantic token naming convention below, mirroring
the same intent as `ios-swift-rules`' `design-tokens-accessibility.mdc`
— not a third-party token library.

## Semantic tokens, not raw values

- Colors, spacing, and typography are referenced through
  `MaterialTheme.colorScheme`/`MaterialTheme.typography`/a semantic
  `Spacing` object defined once in `designsystem/` — never raw hex
  literals (`Color(0xFF...)`) or magic `dp` numbers scattered across
  features.
- Define the app's color scheme via Material 3's `ColorScheme` (ideally
  generated from a source color with `dynamicColorScheme`/Material You
  support) rather than hard-coded per-composable colors — this also
  gets light/dark mode handled for free.

## Scalable text

- Use `sp` units (not `dp`) for all text sizes so they scale with the
  user's system font size setting — never a fixed `dp`-based text size.
- Test layouts at the largest system font scale during development, not
  only at the default scale — this is the single most common
  accessibility regression in Compose apps, same as iOS's Dynamic Type
  gap.

## TalkBack

- Every interactive element has a meaningful `contentDescription` —
  icon-only `IconButton`s especially, since TalkBack otherwise reads the
  icon's resource name or nothing at all.
- Group decorative/redundant child elements with
  `Modifier.semantics(mergeDescendants = true)` so TalkBack doesn't read
  a card's contents as disconnected fragments.
- Purely decorative images use `contentDescription = null` explicitly —
  do not leave TalkBack announcing meaningless decoration, and do not
  leave the parameter unset (which is a lint warning, not a deliberate
  choice).

## Accessibility checks (Compose-native, zero third-party)

- Use Compose's semantic-tree test assertions
  (`assertContentDescriptionEquals`, `onNodeWithContentDescription`) in
  at least one instrumented test per critical screen
  (`testing-verify-flows.mdc` gate 6) — this catches missing
  content descriptions programmatically instead of a manual checklist.
- Minimum tappable target size is 48x48dp per Material Design guidance —
  `Modifier.sizeIn(minWidth = 48.dp, minHeight = 48.dp)` on custom
  controls that are visually smaller than that.

## Anti-patterns

- **Raw `Color(0xFF...)` or hex strings** inline in a composable instead
  of a `MaterialTheme.colorScheme` reference.
- **Fixed `dp`-based text sizing** instead of `sp`.
- **Icon-only `IconButton`s with no `contentDescription`.**
- **Skipping the semantic-tree accessibility assertions** in CI instead
  of fixing the underlying issue they'd flag.

